;; Crisp Hand-rolled MMA Matmul (bf16) on NVIDIA: C[M x N] = A[M x K] . B[K x N], f32 accumulate.
;; Section 1, Chapter 1 — the FLOOR of the NVIDIA 16-bit ladder.
;;
;; WHY THIS RUNG EXISTS.  Until endeavour 159 Phase B the PTX backend could not emit a 16-bit MMA
;; at all (both paths hardcoded tf32), so every `_bf16` chapter kernel in this tree was an Intel
;; one -- `matmul_bmg_bf16.crisp` -- and the NVIDIA 16-bit ladder had no rungs whatsoever.  This is
;; the first.
;;
;; DELIBERATELY A LINE-FOR-LINE PORT of chap1_handrolled_mma/matmul.crisp.  Same hand-rolled loop,
;; same tile geometry, same explicit load-tile-at; ONLY the operand element type and the K-step
;; differ.  A difference between this row and the tf32 row is therefore the FORMAT, not a different
;; kernel wearing the same name -- which is the whole point of a ladder whose rungs are comparable.
;;
;; K-STEP IS 16, NOT 8.  The Hopper ladder is m16n8k8 (tf32) -> m16n8k16 (bf16/fp16): K doubles,
;; M and N do not.  That is why the 16-bit ceiling is ~2x tf32 rather than 4x, which endeavour
;; 159 Phase A measured and confirmed on this part.
;;
;; OPERANDS STAGE THROUGH SHARED MEMORY, and must on NVIDIA.  Endeavour 142's register-resident
;; operand path (load-tile straight into a register tile) lowers to Subgroup2DBlockLoadINTEL and is
;; Intel-only; on NVIDIA it is a compile-time refusal.
;;
;; THE ACCUMULATOR IS f32 -- a 16-bit MMA accumulates in fp32 on both vendors.  bf16 has no
;; f16-accumulate analogue at all, so there is not even a tempting wrong option here.
;;
;; EXPECT THIS TO BE SLOW, and read it as the floor rather than as a result.  It is the sync MMA
;; with one warp per block and no pipelining: no cp.async, no ring, no warp specialization.  Each
;; rung above it adds exactly one technique, and chap6 (warp specialization) is where the NVIDIA
;; sync-MMA ladder actually gets competitive -- endeavour 139 measured ws2 as the fastest Crisp
;; kernel of its day, 2x the pipelined kernel at N=1024, all without wgmma.

(def-type a-mat (matrix bfloat16 :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :row-major))
(def-type b-mat (matrix bfloat16 :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :col-major))
(def-type c-mat (matrix float    :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :row-major))

(def-kernel matmul (A B &out C)
  (declare #'(a-mat b-mat &out c-mat)
           (global-size :derive-from C :strategy :strided)
           (local-size :set-to 32))
  (tile-stride C (64 64) (grid-y grid-x)
    (let ((A-tile (make-scratch-matrix bfloat16 (64 16)))   ; M x K, one bf16 K-step
          (B-tile (make-scratch-matrix bfloat16 (16 64)))   ; K x N
          (C-tile (make-register-tile float (64 64) 0.0))
          (K      (inner-dimension A B)))
      (dotimes (kt (/ K (to-ulong 16)))
        (load-tile-at A A-tile ((* grid-y (to-ulong 64)) (* kt (to-ulong 16))))
        (load-tile-at B B-tile ((* kt (to-ulong 16)) (* grid-x (to-ulong 64))))
        (sync-workgroup)
        (mma-accumulate-via-tile (16 8 16) C-tile A-tile B-tile)
        (sync-workgroup))
      :epilogue
      (store-tile C-tile C (grid-y grid-x)))))
